===============================================================================
ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS
===============================================================================

1. ORIGINAL WORK ATTRIBUTION:
   The above copyright notice for Sebastian Lague and this permission notice 
   shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.
   
   Any use of the original ray tracing foundation must acknowledge:
   "Based on Sebastian Lague's Ray Tracing implementation"
   "Original project: https://github.com/SebLague/Ray-Tracing"

2. ACADEMIC WORK ATTRIBUTION:
   Any use, modification, or distribution that includes the relativistic 
   physics extensions must acknowledge the academic research contribution:
   
   "Relativistic extensions developed for SIBGRAPI 2026 research"
   
   For academic citations, use:
   ```
   @inproceedings{relativistic_raytracer_2026,
     title={Real-Time Relativistic Ray Tracing in Unity: A Comparative Study 
            of Schwarzschild and Kerr Metrics},
     author={Artur Raffael Cavalcanti and Lucas Silva Figueiredo},
     booktitle={Proceedings of SIBGRAPI 2026},
     year={2026},
     organization={UFRPE}
   }
   ```

3. RESEARCH INTEGRITY REQUIREMENTS:
   
   a) ACADEMIC USE: Any academic publication, thesis, dissertation, or research 
      paper that uses this software or its concepts must:
      - Cite both the original work (Sebastian Lague) and the academic 
        extensions (SIBGRAPI 2026 research)
      - Acknowledge the specific relativistic physics implementations
      - Reference the benchmark methodology if used
   
   b) COMMERCIAL USE: Commercial applications may use this software but must:
      - Include both copyright notices in documentation
      - Acknowledge the academic research foundation
      - Not claim original authorship of the relativistic physics algorithms
   
   c) DERIVATIVE RESEARCH: Any derivative academic work must:
      - Clearly distinguish new contributions from existing work
      - Maintain proper attribution chain
      - Share improvements with the research community when published

===============================================================================
RESEARCH DATA AND METHODOLOGY PROTECTION
===============================================================================

4. BENCHMARK DATA PROTECTION:
   The benchmark methodology, test configurations, and measurement techniques 
   developed for this research are protected academic contributions. Any use 
   of similar benchmark approaches should cite this work appropriately.

5. PHYSICS IMPLEMENTATION PROTECTION:
   The specific implementations of Schwarzschild and Kerr metrics, numerical 
   integration methods, and relativistic ray marching algorithms represent 
   novel academic contributions and should be cited when used or adapted.
